#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:2
msgid "Public, private and unlisted-snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:4
msgid ""
"Alongside using {ref}`tracks and channels <explanation-how-snaps-work-"
"channels-and-tracks>` to control which releases are available, and "
"restrictions per-territory, Snap developers can also control _who_ has "
"access to their snaps by marking a published snap as either public, private "
"or unlisted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:6
msgid ""
"When [registering a snap](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/latest/"
"how-to/publishing/register-a-snap/), there is an option to make its listing "
"either public or private. After registration, this value can be changed from "
"the _Settings page_ of the Snap Store web UI  for the  registered snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:8
msgid ""
"![Snap Store settings tab](https://assets.ubuntu.com/v1/617fa9e2-"
"private_03.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:8
msgid "Snap Store settings tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:10
msgid "A snap's  _Visibility_ settings can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:12
msgid ""
"**Unlisted**: the snap is omitted from search results but it can still be "
"installed by any user when they explicitly asks for it by name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:13
msgid ""
"**Public** : the snap will appear in local  `snap find`  searches, in the "
"Snap Store, and other application installers that access the store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:14
msgid ""
"**Private** : the snap is hidden from search results, and can only be "
"installed from your account and from accounts linked to your account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:16
msgid ""
"If a previously public snap is made private, installed versions are "
"unaffected. However, those snaps will no longer receive updates, and if the "
"user removes them, they can't be re-installed from the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:18
msgid ""
"Access to a private snap can be shared by adding individual email addresses "
"to the text field on the _Collaboration_ page of a snap's "
"[dashboard.snapcraft.io](https://dashboard.snapcraft.io/) entry:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:20
msgid ""
"![Snap Store private settings](https://assets.ubuntu.com/v1/74e9f011-"
"private_02.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:20
msgid "Snap Store private settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:22
msgid "Visibility from snapcraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:24
msgid ""
"With [Snapcraft](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/) "
"installed and logged-in to a developer account, the _snapcraft names_ "
"command can be used to check the visibility status of snaps associated with "
"the developer account:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/public-private-unlisted-snaps.md:26
msgid ""
"$ snapcraft names\n"
"Name             Since                 Visibility    Notes\n"
"cameractrls      2022-11-28T18:15:44Z  public        -\n"
"domoticz         2020-01-17T17:21:43Z  public        -\n"
msgstr ""
